\tab\tab\tab\tab routine is also part of this file.\par
\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab Note: Future releases of P?S/8 may reduce this\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab file to merely the keyboard monitor.  By doing\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab this, these separate system programs can be better\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab explained.  Even using the present mechanism to\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab create the starter system (and extending it to\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab include most of the rest of the system programs\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab later) does not require these other system program\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab components to be functional or even available,\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab albeit highly recommended.  As such, a better\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab overall mechanism can relegate the creation of all\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab of them to whatever ultimate process is used to\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab create the overall system.\cf1\par
\par
\cf0 3)\tab PQSDTA.BN\tab\tab This is the image of the system device handler for \tab\tab\tab\tab TC01/TC08/TU55/TU56.  Since this device also \tab\tab\tab\tab\tab supports a \i Slurp\i0  loader, the image of the\par
 \tab\tab\tab\tab hardware-dependent \i Slurp\i0  loader is included.\par
\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab Note: For systems that do not support a hardware-\par
\tab\tab\tab\tab dependent \i Slurp\i0  loader, the system generation\par
 \tab\tab\tab\tab routines write out a deliberately non-functional\par
 \tab\tab\tab\tab dummy program stub to cause attempts to load a \tab\tab\tab\tab\tab hardware-dependent \i Slurp\i0  loader to instead use the\par
