08-Aug-2015\tab Keyboard monitor bug fix.\par
\par
Problem: Keyboard monitor commands that support both an optional \cf3\i :u \cf0\i0 suffix and an optional \cf3\i filename\cf0\i0  [such as EN\{ter\}, FE\{tch\}, KI\{ll\} and WR\{ite\}] fail to properly support the \cf3\i filename\cf0\i0  when both options are used simultaneously.\par
\par
Note: The problem also exists if the \cf3\i filename:u\cf0\i0  form is used; however, the second \cf3\i :u\cf0\i0  suffix is unrelated to the problem.\par
\par
In most instances, the optional \cf3\i :u \cf0\i0 suffix is rarely used.  When the optional \cf3\i filename\cf0\i0  is not present, the default name from a prior command is used as the file name for the current command:\par
\par
.FE FOOBAR\tab\cf1 The explicit file name used sets the default name.\cf0\par
\par
\cf1 [Some editing operations are performed to update the file contents.]\cf0\par
\par
.WR\tab\tab\tab\cf1 The updated file is written using the default name.\par
\cf0\par
Alternatively, the command\par
\par
.WR:1\par
\par
writes the file to logical device unit 1 with the same file name.\par
\par
Since there is no explicit file name in either WR\{ite\} command example, both commands function as expected.\par
\par
However, if both options are used in the same command such as\par
\par
.WR:1 FOOBAR\par
\par
the command will fail to complete properly and will likely lead to an error message.\par
\par
Note: The contents of the edit buffer are not affected by the problem.  A similar command with only one of the options or no options given will succeed without error.\page\cf1 P?S/8 Version 8Z Change Log (continued).\par
\cf0\par
